What to do next

solana: Clipper 1.4.0 is checked; an upload builds the release APK signed with your dApp Store key (versionCode 42) and submits it for review with the dapp-store tool. Its screenshots are checked: 4 images for solana-previews. Nothing was built or sent.

  1. Create the Publisher Portal account and the publisher profile, and pass KYC (individual) or KYB (company). (you, the account holder)
     Open   https://publish.solanamobile.com
     Why by hand: identity verification has no API, and needs the account holder
     Done when: the portal lets you add a dApp

  2. Connect the publisher wallet in the portal: a new Solana wallet dedicated to publishing, which every future submission of this app must sign with. (you, the account holder)
     Open   https://publish.solanamobile.com
     Wallet address: (set LEPTOSKIT_PUBLISH_SOLANA_KEYPAIR to a funded Solana keypair)
     Why by hand: wallet custody is the account holder's, and losing the wallet blocks every future submission
     Done when: the portal shows the wallet connected

  3. Create the app in the portal: the app details form and its listing images.
     Open   https://publish.solanamobile.com
     Package name: com.example.clipper
     Name: Clipper
     Short description: Clip quotes from anything you read.
     Website: https://clipper.example
     Support email: help@clipper.example
     Terms of Use: (a public HTTPS page the portal checks)
     Privacy policy: https://clipper.example/privacy
     Icon: store/screenshots/solana-icon/*.png (512×512, no transparency)
     Banner: store/screenshots/solana-banner/*.png (1200×600)
     Previews: store/screenshots/solana-previews/*.png (4 to 8, all one size)
     Why by hand: the first app and its listing are created in the portal; the official tool only updates an app that already exists there, matched by the package name
     Done when: the app exists with its App NFT minted

  4. Approve the App NFT mint transaction in the connected wallet, and every signing request the portal raises after it. (you, the account holder)
     Open   https://publish.solanamobile.com
     Why by hand: the mint is a Solana transaction only the wallet's holder can sign
     Done when: the portal shows the app's App NFT minted

  5. Create the portal API key, and set it as LEPTOSKIT_PUBLISH_SOLANA_API_KEY. (you, the account holder)
     Open   https://publish.solanamobile.com/dashboard/settings/api-keys
     Why by hand: an API key is created by the signed-in account holder
     Done when: `leptoskit publish credentials` lists it as set

  6. Fund the publishing wallet with about 0.02 SOL; the dapp-store tool refuses to start below 0.016 SOL, which minting the release NFT costs. (you, the account holder)
     Wallet address: (set LEPTOSKIT_PUBLISH_SOLANA_KEYPAIR to a funded Solana keypair)
     Why by hand: only the wallet's holder can move its SOL
     Done when: `leptoskit publish solana` gets past the balance check

  7. Add what the app's listing is missing to the project, and upload again.
     Open   https://publish.solanamobile.com
     Icon: (put one 512×512 image in store/screenshots/solana-icon/)
     Banner: (put one 1200×600 image in store/screenshots/solana-banner/)
     Why by hand: the portal's listing form and its images have no API, and the official tool takes none of them
     Done when: the portal's listing shows them

  8. Decide to release it, then run `leptoskit publish solana --submit`, which submits the release for review. (you, the account holder)
     Release: .leptoskit/publish/solana/app-release.apk
     Why by hand: submitting mints the release NFT and sends the app to review, which is the account holder's decision
     Done when: the portal shows the release in review
